From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:40:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-glymur: Model the USB4 PHY RX and P2RR2P muxes
 as PHY muxes

The USB4 PHY P2RR2P pipe, RX0 and RX1 clock sources choose between a
clock generated by the USB4 PHY (value 0) and TCXO (value 2). The driver
describes them as plain regmap muxes whose PHY parent is not provided in
the device tree, so the framework never moves them: they stay wherever
the boot firmware left them, also while the PHY is off and its clock is
gone.

Describe them with clk_regmap_phy_mux, as gcc-x1e80100 does for the same
muxes, so that they select the PHY clock while enabled and are parked on
TCXO otherwise. Drop the parent maps that are no longer used.

Fixes: efe504300a17 ("clk: qcom: gcc: Add support for Global Clock Controller")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
